{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"mission":1,"hero":505},{"id":2,"agency":3,"agency_full":4,"sector":5,"dest":6,"color":7,"year":8,"status":9,"departure_date":10,"arrival_date":11,"transit_days":12,"vehicle":13,"payload":14,"delta_v":15,"data_quality":16,"credit":17,"links":18,"flight_data_quality":30,"fleet_refs":31,"flight":37,"name":481,"type":482,"first":483,"description":484,"events":485,"vehicle_stage":39},"mangalyaan","ISRO","Indian Space Research Organisation","gov","MARS","#FF9933",2013,"FLOWN","2013-11-05","2014-09-24",323,"PSLV-XL (C25)","1337 kg","~3.5 km/s","good","© ISRO. India's first interplanetary mission, succeeded on first attempt — at one-tenth the cost of MAVEN. Communication ended April 2022 after its propellant ran out and its battery drained below its safe limit during long eclipses (ISRO).",[19,23,26],{"l":20,"u":21,"t":22},"Mars Orbiter Mission — Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Orbiter_Mission","intro",{"l":24,"u":25,"t":22},"MOM (ISRO)","https://www.isro.gov.in/MarsOrbiterMissionSpacecraft.html",{"l":27,"u":28,"t":29},"मंगलयान — हिन्दी विकिपीडिया","https://hi.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%82%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%B2%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A8","core","measured",[32,35],{"id":33,"role":34},"pslv-xl","launcher",{"id":2,"role":36},"spacecraft",{"launch":38,"cruise":42,"arrival":45,"totals":51,"events":55,"interplanetary_profile":91},{"vehicle_stage":39,"mass_at_tli_kg":40,"source":41,"departure":36},"PSLV PS4 fourth stage",1337,"ISRO MOM Mission Report (2014); MOM used multi-burn Earth-orbit raising before TMI",{"tcm_count":43,"source":44},4,"ISRO MOM Mission Operations Report",{"v_infinity_km_s":46,"periapsis_km":47,"inclination_deg":48,"orbit_insertion_dv_km_s":49,"source":50},2.65,421,150,1.1,"ISRO MOM MOI Report (2014-09); highly elliptical orbit",{"total_dv_km_s":52,"tli_or_tmi_dv_km_s":53,"source":54},3.5,1.45,"ISRO MOM Mission Report (2014); low TMI ∆v due to Earth-orbit raising strategy",[56,61,66,71,75,77,81,86],{"met_days":57,"type":58,"label":59,"description":60},0,"launch","Launch — PSLV-XL","Sriharikota, India, 2013-11-05. Mangalyaan (Mars Orbiter Mission, MOM) — ISRO's first interplanetary mission, launched on a Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle that lacked the energy for a direct Mars transfer. Solution: launch into Earth orbit and use 6 successive perigee burns to raise apogee until a final TMI burn could be done from a highly-elliptical Earth orbit.",{"met_days":62,"type":63,"label":64,"description":65},25.43,"tli_or_tmi","Trans-Mars injection","2013-11-30. After six Earth-orbit-raising burns, a separate 23-minute trans-Mars injection burn sent Mangalyaan onto a heliocentric Mars-transfer trajectory. Total mission cost was just $74M, the least expensive Mars mission to succeed.",{"met_days":67,"type":68,"label":69,"description":70},50,"tcm","TCM-1","First post-TMI cruise correction.",{"met_days":72,"type":68,"label":73,"description":74},97.62,"TCM-2","Mid-cruise refinement.",{"met_days":48,"type":68,"label":76,"description":74},"TCM-3",{"met_days":78,"type":68,"label":79,"description":80},250,"TCM-4 — final pre-MOI burn","Final approach targeting before Mars orbit insertion.",{"met_days":82,"type":83,"label":84,"description":85},324,"arrival","Mars approach","Pre-MOI checkout phase. 2014-09-24 arrival — 2 days after NASA's MAVEN reached Mars orbit; India became the 4th space agency to reach Mars and the first to succeed on its first attempt.",{"met_days":87,"type":88,"label":89,"description":90},324.005,"edl_or_oi","Mars orbit insertion","24-minute main engine burn captured Mangalyaan into a highly-elliptical 421.7 × 76,994 km orbit. The mission was designed for 6 months but operated for ~8 years at Mars before contact was lost in 2022.",{"source_tier":92,"reference_frame":93,"departure_body":94,"arrival_body":95,"transfer_type":96,"tcm_count":43,"waypoints_helio_au":97},"tier_1_5_hybrid","heliocentric_ecliptic_J2000","earth","mars","type1_lambert",[98,101,